meta {
  name: Media Service Health
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/healthz
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  # Media Service Health Check
  
  Check the health status of all services including S3-backed media storage.
  
  ## Response Fields:
  - `status`: Overall system status (ok, degraded, error)
  - `timestamp`: Current server timestamp
  - `uptime`: Server uptime in seconds
  - `environment`: Current environment (development, production)
  - `services`: Object containing status of each service
  
  ## Service Statuses:
  - `database`: PostgreSQL connection status
  - `webrtc`: Socket.IO signaling service status
  - `storage`: Media upload service status
  - `environment`: Environment configuration status
  
  ## Storage Status Values:
  - `connected`: S3 bucket is reachable and public media URLs are accessible
  - `warning`: S3 credentials not configured (media uploads disabled)
  - `error`: Bucket access failed or returned public media URLs are not reachable
  
  ## HTTP Status Codes:
  - `200`: All services healthy
  - `503`: One or more services degraded or failed
}
